Z||000000||fieroshop||08-10-2000||06:38 PM||||Went to the first annual Northwest Fiero Fest in Richland, Washington. There were six cars (that is what I was told) in the custom modified class and the first three places ther was a half point difference. <BR>I ended up wit the longest distance car and also took third place. Considering that my GT was still apart the day that I left for Washington, I did real good. <BR>Here are a few pics That I took. The first one is mine.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88_GT1.jpg"> <BR>The red one is John Szpara's GT.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Both_1.jpg"> <BR>Here is a sight, hardly ever seen.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Yellow_Cars.jpg"> <BR>I will post more pictures as I find them.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Wolfhound||08-10-2000||07:13 PM||||George, Your GT really looks classy with the new paint and wheels.   <BR> What is the story on the odd hood on the red Fiero, on the left in the above photo.<BR>Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||5
